#: ../../ops/hub.rst:666
msgid ""
"There is no route that restores a deleted registration from an archive, "
"because that would write an old key history back into the registry. To "
"undo a deletion, run ``anet-hub admit <AID>``; the node re-registers the "
"next time ``anet hub-register`` runs. Other paths under ``/admin/api/`` "
"answer ``404`` with a JSON body after authentication. The console itself "
"is served as a single page. ``GET /admin/healthz`` reports the version, "
"commit and build time of the operator plane without authentication, so "
"that a deployment can confirm which build is running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/hub.rst:675
msgid ""
"The official-agent register is read at start from ``officials.json`` in "
"the operator plane's data directory; a missing file means no official "
"agents. An entry that still carries ``runtime``, ``monitor``, ``ops`` or "
"``datasets`` fields is refused, and the process does not start. The "
"operator plane starts, stops or updates no agent; those tasks belong to "
"separate tooling outside the hub host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/hub.rst:684
msgid ""
"The console is being redesigned as a navigation sidebar with sections for"
" overview, nodes, registration, federation, settlement and audit, "
"admission and quota, and logs, with sortable and filterable tables. "
"Delivery confirmations and admission state (proof of work, quota, "
"probation) are shown there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/hub.rst:690
msgid ""
"Two options of earlier releases, ``--restore-agents-from`` and ``--keep-"
"only-agents``, are removed. Each is refused with exit status 2 and names "
"its replacement (``anet-hub restore`` and the console's delete function "
"or ``anet-hub admissions revoke``)."
msgstr ""

